# Commit Message Standards

Follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/) as `@commitlint/config-conventional` defines them. Lefthook `prepare-commit-msg` prepends `[ENG-n]` from the branch name when present.

**Format:** `[ENG-n] <type>([optional scope]): <description>`

The `[ENG-n]` prefix is optional for commitlint (`feat(ics): …` still passes). On ticket branches it is injected automatically. Do not use a `feature` type alias.

## Allowed Commit Types

- `feat` — new capability
- `fix` — bug fix
- `docs` — documentation only (e.g. README, `.cursor/rules/`)
- `style` — formatting changes that do not affect logic
- `refactor` — neither fix nor feat
- `perf` — performance improvement
- `test` — add or correct tests
- `build` — build system or external dependencies
- `ci` — CI configuration and scripts
- `chore` — other tooling that is not `build` or `ci`
- `revert` — revert a previous commit

## Scopes

Prefer domain scopes: `lunar-dates`, `ics`, `store`, `wizard`, `cart`, `preview`, `App`, `hooks`, `ui`.

## Ticket prefix

Extract the first `ENG-\d+` from the branch name (case-insensitive) and prepend `[ENG-n] `. Skip prefix injection on `develop`, `staging`, `release`, and `release/*`.

## Breaking Changes

Use `BREAKING CHANGE:` in the footer, or `!` after the type/scope (e.g. `feat!:`).

## Examples

- `[ENG-27] feat(ics): add all-day lunar milestone calendar export`
- `[ENG-27] ci: update precommit hook`
- `fix(lunar-dates): use UTC date parts for ICS DATE values`
- `test(lunar-dates): cover leap-month 初一 notifications`
- `docs: clarify cursor rules and file sizing caps`
